{title: 019 - O Sing a New Song to the Lord}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #019 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 19}
{meta: category Worship - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]O [Em]sing [Am/C]a [D]new [D7/C]song [G/B]to [Am]the [G]Lord
[D]For [G]marvels He [Em]has [D]done;
[D]His [G]right [D]hand [Em]and [Bm]His [C]holy [D]arm
[D7/C]The [G/B]victory have [D7]won.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]With [Em]harp, [Am/C]and [D7/C]voice [G/B]of [Am]psalms
[D]Unto [G]Jehovah [D]sing;
[D]Let [G]trumpets [Em]and [Bm]the [C]echoing [D]horn
[D7/C]Acclaim [C]the Lord [G/D]our [D7]King!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]Let seas [Em]with [Am/C]all [D]their [D7/C]creatures [G]roar,
[D]The [G]world and dwellers [D]there,
[D]And [G]let [D]the [Em]rivers [C]clap [Am]their [D]hands,
[D7/C]The [G/B]hills [C]their joy [G/D]declare.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[G]Before [Em]the [Am/C]Lord: [D]because [G/B]He [Am]comes,
[D]To [G]judge the earth [Em]come [D]He;
[D]He'll judge [Bm]the [Am]world
[D]with righteousness,
[D7/C]His [G/B]folk [C]with equity.
{end_of_verse}
